  "invariants": {
    "INV-01_NAMESPACE_PREFIX": "Every decision_time_fields entry starts with 'dt.', execution_time_fields with 'ex.', outcome_time_fields with 'oc.'.",
    "INV-02_NAMESPACE_DISJOINT": "The three time-namespace lists of an experiment are pairwise disjoint, and no 'ex.' or 'oc.' field appears in frozen_rule.decision_inputs.",
    "INV-03_REJECTED_FAMILY_LINKAGE": "A STRUCTURAL_VARIANT_OF edge whose parent is closed rejected or quarantined is permitted only when structural_difference, new_task_id and new_model_identity are all present and non-empty.",
    "INV-04_PROVENANCE_PRESERVED": "Every experiment references at least one existing data_source_id; every result references an existing experiment_id; retained_path and evidence_paths are copied verbatim and never rewritten by the builder.",
    "INV-05_SECONDARY_EVIDENCE_DOWNGRADE": "A SECONDARY_DOC or SECONDARY_CHAT source describing an evidence_type for which a RAW_PRIMARY source exists must name that source in superseded_by_raw_source_id.",
    "INV-06_NO_PROMOTION": "verdict ADMITTED_RESEARCH_ONLY requires every declared gate PASS and a non-empty validator_id; the catalogue always reports promising_count = 0.",
    "INV-07_EXPLICIT_ROOTS_ONLY": "The builder reads only from roots supplied explicitly on the command line, or the committed synthetic fixture in smoke mode. Home, repository root and filesystem root are refused.",
    "INV-08_SMOKE_NON_MUTATION": "Smoke mode performs no filesystem write of any kind. Output requires an explicit --out path.",
    "INV-09_TRIAL_COUNT_CONSERVATION": "For every experiment declaring prior_trials_seeded, that value equals the sum of exact_trial_count over the counting ledger entries linked to it. A ledger entry must name an existing parent experiment.",
    "INV-10_AGGREGATE_CHILD_EXCLUSIVITY": "A trial cannot be counted twice. Among counting entries every dedup_key is unique. An entry naming member_of_aggregate_trial_id must be non-counting, and the aggregate it names must exist and be AGGREGATE_ONLY.",
    "INV-11_NO_FABRICATED_VARIANT": "Every ledger entry needs a real evidence_path; placeholder values are refused. An AGGREGATE_ONLY entry must carry a null parameter_fingerprint, because a per-variant fingerprint derived from an aggregate count would be invented. A fingerprint whose text declares it inferred, assumed, or generated is refused.",
    "INV-12_MISSING_EVIDENCE_DECLARED": "An entry whose reconciliation_status is AGGREGATE_PENDING_CHILDREN or UNRECOVERABLE_PENDING_SOURCE must name an existing trial_evidence record stating exactly which artefact would reconcile it.",
    "INV-13_ATTACKS_DO_NOT_ADD_TRIALS": "A ROBUSTNESS_ATTACK, NULL_CONTROL or REPLAY entry is never counting, must name the trial it attacks, and that trial must exist under the same parent experiment. Re-attacking a parameter point does not consume a new independent trial.",
    "INV-14_IDENTITY_IS_NOT_A_MEASUREMENT": "A mechanical_identity is true by construction: it carries no n, t_stat, ci, null_test, oos or remove_best, and its status is 'proven'. An empirical_market_law is the opposite: it must carry n, t_stat and a confidence interval, must declare all three checks explicitly (PASS, FAIL or NOT_RUN), and may never hold status 'proven'. This exists so nobody applies a t-test to an arithmetic identity.",
    "INV-15_REPLICATION_REQUIRES_THE_CHECKS": "An empirical_market_law may reach status 'replicated' only when null_test, oos and remove_best are all PASS. With any check NOT_RUN or FAIL the status stays 'observed' or worse.",
    "INV-16_CONSTRAINTS_ARE_SCOPED": "A data_constraint names the specific data_source ids it applies to, and each must exist. A constraint may not be stated globally over an entire evidence class.",
    "INV-17_LAWS_CITE_THEIR_SOURCES": "Every market_law references at least one existing data_source, names a transform_version, and records its tested variants including the negative ones.",
    "INV-18": "Every closure_decision names a decisive measurement and a reopen criterion, and every law_id and constraint_id it cites must exist in the catalogue."
  },
